  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|1\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 0| \\\\  & =|-2-0| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
